        {
          "comments": "NOT REVIEWED — raw running config supplied for manual review; no automated pass, finding, or applicability decision asserted.",
          "finding_details": "Raw running config SHA-256: 8ed0c9e3e59ab6fc8afc4e5e20d238df8b4935a3640646cb62cedeb5ef3f3654\nOfficial Cisco benchmark SHA-256: cea38d4f4c305fd029377fd56916560a0ef73afcdeed347bb17ace704928281c\nRunning config alone does not verify this control's complete operational check; manual review required.",
          "fix_text": "Configure the Cisco ASA to use at least two authentication servers as shown in the following example.\n\nStep 1: Define the authentication group and protocol.\n\nASA(config)# aaa-server RADIUS_GROUP protocol radius\n\nStep 2: Define the authentication servers. \n\nASA(config)# aaa-server RADIUS_GROUP (NDM_INTERFACE) host 10.1.48.10         \nASA(config-aaa-server-host)# key bobby\nASA(config-aaa-server-host)# exit\nASA(config)# aaa-server RADIUS_GROUP (NDM_INTERFACE) host 10.1.48.11         \nASA(config-aaa-server-host)# key bobby2\nASA(config-aaa-server-host)# exit\n\nStep 3: Use the AAA server for login authentication for both in-band and console access methods.\n\nASA(config)# aaa authentication serial console RADIUS_GROUP LOCAL\nASA(config)# aaa authentication ssh console RADIUS_GROUP LOCAL\nASA(config)# end",
          "group_id": "V-239940",
          "group_id_src": "V-239940",
          "group_title": "SRG-APP-000516-NDM-000336",
          "rule_id": "SV-239940r1137887_rule",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-239940r1137887_rule",
          "rule_title": "The Cisco ASA must be configured to use at least two authentication servers to authenticate users prior to granting administrative access.",
          "rule_version": "CASA-ND-001310",
          "severity": "high",
          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "stig_uuid": "e29d3fd3-66fb-55b8-88d4-3841c0905725",
          "uuid": "b63a9734-567d-5b6d-8232-7740f108cfa9",
          "weight": "10.0"
        },
        {
          "comments": "NOT REVIEWED — raw running config supplied for manual review; no automated pass, finding, or applicability decision asserted.",
          "finding_details": "Raw running config SHA-256: 8ed0c9e3e59ab6fc8afc4e5e20d238df8b4935a3640646cb62cedeb5ef3f3654\nOfficial Cisco benchmark SHA-256: cea38d4f4c305fd029377fd56916560a0ef73afcdeed347bb17ace704928281c\nRunning config alone does not verify this control's complete operational check; manual review required.",
          "fix_text": "Configure the Cisco ASA to send the configuration to an SCP server when a configuration change occurs as shown in the example below.\n\nASA(config)# event manager applet BACKUP_CONFIG\nASA(config-applet)# event syslog id 111010\nASA(config-applet)# action 1 cli command \" copy startup-config scp://userx:xxxxxxx@10.1.48.10//opt/config_backup”\nASA(config-applet)# action 2 syslog priority informational msg \"Configuration backup was executed\"\nASA(config-applet)# end",
          "group_id": "V-239941",
          "group_id_src": "V-239941",
          "group_title": "SRG-APP-000516-NDM-000340",
